<title>USA: Suzuki verdict reversed by Missouri court.</title>
<headline>Suzuki verdict reversed by Missouri court.</headline>
<dateline>BREA, Calif. 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Suzuki Motor Corp said the Missouri Supreme Court reversed a $90 million jury verdict against the company in a lawsuit brought by a woman who was seriously injured in a Suzuki Samurai sport utility vehicle.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the reversal was based on the court's ruling that evidence of alcohol consumption, barred from the previous trial, could be admitted as evidence.</p>
<p>The plaintiff in the trial, Kathryn Rodriguez, could not be immediately reached for comment.</p>
</text>
